# ============================================================================
# users.conf.example — atmoz/sftp account list  (EXAMPLE ONLY)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXAMPLE ONLY — the live ./users.conf is GENERATED by scripts/setup.sh / the
# API sync layer from the project accounts config; never hand-edit the live
# file. The live users.conf is git-ignored (§11.4.10); this tracked .example
# is the reference template (whitelisted in .gitignore).
#
# Line grammar (atmoz/sftp — evidence: docs/research/mvp/MVP.md lines 62-71):
#   user:password:uid:gid:home_directory[:options]
#   * one account per line
#   * home_directory is a path INSIDE the container; with ./data bind-mounted
#     at /sftp_data (deploy/docker-compose.yml), each home is
#     /sftp_data/<username> and the host dir must be owned by the same
#     numeric uid:gid (MVP.md lines 117-132)
#   * password is stored as plain text in the live file (MVP.md "Security
#     Note", line 221); for key-only accounts the password field may be `*`
#     (MVP.md line 235)
#   * the $6$example$... values below are placeholder-shaped sha512-crypt
#     look-alikes, NOT valid hashes — real credentials never live in git
#     (§11.4.10)
#
# Permission model (project layer; full semantics in the accounts-config
# README once its home is decided — see qa/results/STREAM-3-report.md):
#   read_only  — chrooted into home; write-masked (download only)
#   read_write — chrooted into home; owns its dir (upload + download)
#   public     — NEVER default; only with public_acknowledged: true upstream
#
# The 3 lines below mirror the 3 example accounts of the project accounts
# config (read_write, read_only, public-commented-out).
# ============================================================================

# read_write — owns its home dir (uid:gid 1002:1002)
sftp_writer:$6$example$CHANGE_ME_writer:1002:1002:/sftp_data/sftp_writer

# read_only — write-masked home (uid:gid 1001:1001)
sftp_reader:$6$example$CHANGE_ME_reader:1001:1001:/sftp_data/sftp_reader

# public — DISABLED by default (public is never default, project rule);
# rendered only when the accounts config carries public_acknowledged: true:
# sftp_public:$6$example$CHANGE_ME_public:1003:1003:/sftp_data/sftp_public
